Why Is Demand Increasing
Minimally Invasive Treatment — TAVR provides a catheter-based alternative to conventional open-heart valve replacement for appropriately selected patients, supporting continued adoption of less-invasive structural-heart procedures.
Aortic Stenosis Burden — The prevalence of aortic valve disease, particularly among aging populations, is creating a growing clinical need for valve replacement procedures.
Device Innovation — Improvements in valve design, delivery systems, positioning, sealing, and procedural imaging are expanding the capabilities of transcatheter interventions.

Clinical & Reimbursement Watch: Structural Heart Care Expands
TAVR adoption is closely linked to patient selection, clinical evidence, hospital infrastructure, specialist expertise, reimbursement frameworks, and access to structural-heart programs. Continued device development is also supporting broader procedural capabilities and the treatment of increasingly diverse patient populations.

